```css
/* @theme my-extended-theme */

@import 'default';

section {
  background-color: #f0f0f0;
}
```

You can extend existing themes.

```css
/* @theme my-theme */

@import-theme 'default';

h1 {
  color: red;
}
```

Using `@import-theme` allows loading by theme name.

```css
section.lead {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  text-align: center;
}

section.lead h1 {
  font-size: 64px;
}
```

```css
section.invert {
  background-color: #000;
  color: #fff;
}

section.invert h1,
section.invert h2 {
  color: #fff;
}
```

Use `<style scoped>` in Markdown:

```markdown
<style scoped>
section {
  background-color: #e3f2fd;
}
</style>

# Only this slide has blue background
```

Background images are processed automatically but can be adjusted with CSS:

```css
section[data-marpit-background-image] {
  background-size: cover;
  background-position: center;
}
```

```css
ul, ol {
  margin: 0.5em 0;
  padding-left: 1.5em;
}

li {
  margin: 0.3em 0;
}

li::marker {
  color: #3b82f6;
}
```

```css
table {
  border-collapse: collapse;
  width: 100%;
  margin: 1em 0;
}

th, td {
  border: 1px solid #ddd;
  padding: 0.5em 1em;
  text-align: left;
}

th {
  background-color: #f0f0f0;
  font-weight: bold;
}
```

```css
pre {
  background-color: #f5f5f5;
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 1em;
  overflow-x: auto;
}

code {
  font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
  font-size: 0.9em;
}

pre code {
  background-color: transparent;
  padding: 0;
}
```

```css
@media screen and (max-width: 1280px) {
